(** * Lemma (i) for dynamic blocks: the certificates (one per memLevel) and the bound

    The certificates (cert128 .. cert32768) are generated by docs/huffman-gen/certs.py (gen_cert.py) from the
    dual of a linear program over the facts of [block_facts] (per-code charging; see Cert.v); every certificate
    is checked by computation ([cert_ok]).
    memLevel 1 (lit_bufsize 128) needs the header bound against bit-length codes with the repair overhead of the
    bit-length tree at most 75 bits (block_facts states 100; with 100 the linear program's optimum is about
    1025 > 1014 bits); all other memLevels use block_facts as it is. *)

